Market Challenges
Reconciling bottom-up operational records with direct measurement evidence can be technically demanding. Differences in measurement methodologies, reporting boundaries, and data quality may increase verification time and complicate the preparation of consistent emissions inventories.

Service providers must also coordinate with operating teams, technical specialists, and corporate reporting departments. Establishing clear verification scopes and maintaining consistent documentation across geographically distributed facilities remain important operational challenges.

Market Restraints
Incomplete source records and differences in methane quantification methods can increase audit costs and delay verification assignments. Limited availability of qualified personnel and restricted access to operating facilities may further constrain service delivery.

Integration delays and pricing pressure can also affect purchasing decisions. Some organisations may postpone external verification or initially commission audits for selected facilities before expanding coverage across their operations.

